<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF says won't comment on NTT share sale.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF says won't comment on NTT share sale.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finance Ministry said on Thursday that it would not comment on whether or not it would sell shares of Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp (NTT).</p>
<p>&quot;NTT share sales are included in the budget for this fiscal year but we will not say whether or not we will actually sell NTT shares,&quot; a MOF official said.</p>
<p>The Japanese government has included NTT share sales in its budget over the past several years but has not actually sold any shares since the year to March 31, 1989, due to weakness in the stock market.</p>
